.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Pomeau and Manneville (1980) identified a third route to chaos, distinct from period-doubling and quasi-periodicity: near a tangent (saddle-node) bifurcation, a trajectory spends increasingly long, apparently regular &quot;laminar&quot; episodes near the fixed point about to vanish, each interrupted by a short chaotic burst, with the mean laminar length diverging as a power law as the tangency is approached. LogisticMap&#x27;s period-three window is born at exactly such a tangent bifurcation, at r\approx3.8284; this example iterates the map at values of r just below that threshold and shows both halves of the phenomenon directly: the laminar-then-burst time series itself, and the mean laminar length growing as r approaches the tangency.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/chaos/chaos_metrics/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_intermittency_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/chaos/chaos_metrics/plot_intermittency`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Pomeau-Manneville intermittency: laminar phases and chaotic bursts</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/chaos/chaos_metrics/plot_intermittency`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="While physicskit.chaos.visualizers.divergence.plot_lyapunov_divergence estimates only the largest Lyapunov exponent from a single pair of trajectories, physicskit.chaos.utils.metrics.benettin_lyapunov_spectrum estimates the full spectrum by co-evolving an orthonormal frame Y under the linearized (variational) dynamics \dot{Y} = J(x(t)) Y, where J is the system&#x27;s Jacobian, and periodically re-orthonormalizing it with a QR decomposition, accumulating the log-growth of each axis. It is applied below to the Lorenz and Rossler flows,">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/chaos/chaos_metrics/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_lyapunov_spectrum_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/chaos/chaos_metrics/plot_lyapunov_spectrum`

.. raw:: html

